        "original_id": "40f30516-5079-514e-aad4-5d332340c5d5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies, The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, Middlebury College\n- People: Bernt Julius Muus\n- Topics: student-sending institutions, college founding\n\nFacts:\n- In 1874, St. Olaf College was founded by a group of Norwegian-American immigrant pastors and farmers led by Pastor Bernt Julius Muus.\n- The Centre for Medieval and Renaissance Studies has received students from American institutions including The University of Georgia, Elmhurst College, St. Mary's College of California, St. Mary's College of Maryland, St. Olaf College, William Jewell College, and Middlebury College.",
